# --- ARM cross-toolchain (not asdf-managed) --------------------------------
#
# The firmware is built with arm-none-eabi-gcc, which asdf has no plugin for,
# so it cannot be pinned by a version line here. It still needs to be pinned
# SOMEWHERE, because it is the thing that broke: the baseline went from
# arm-none-eabi-gcc 14 to 16 underneath the tree, gcc 15 had meanwhile added
# -Wunterminated-string-initialization, and the -Werror hw build stopped
# compiling — which nobody noticed for a long time because the only "CI" was
# a stale build directory.
#
# The pin, and where each half is enforced:
#
#   reference toolchain   arm-none-eabi-gcc 14.2.rel1 (Arm GNU Toolchain)
#                         installed by .github/workflows/ci.yml
#                         (ARM_TOOLCHAIN_VERSION / ARM_TOOLCHAIN_URL) in the
#                         firmware-pinned job. Change it in BOTH places.
#
#   floor                 gcc 14. core/meson.build probes for newer-compiler
#                         flags with cc.get_supported_arguments() rather than
#                         passing them blind, so 14 still builds.
#
#   ceiling               none, deliberately. The firmware-rolling CI job
#                         builds against Arch's current arm-none-eabi-gcc
#                         (16.1.0 at the time of writing — what this project's
#                         developers actually run), so the NEXT compiler
#                         upgrade shows up as a red CI run rather than as a
#                         local build that mysteriously stopped working.
#
# See core/cross/arm-none-eabi.txt for the toolchain's build flags.
